# Climbs and descents in a wartime twin.
#
#   name TEXT...                   what the lesson is called
#   teaches CLASS                  which class of aircraft it is for
#   stage TEXT...                  a stage, in the order flown
#   do TEXT...                     what to do at this stage
#   until PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE     what ends the stage
#   hold PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT... a band that must hold for the whole stage
#   need PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE TEXT...  what must be true by the stage's end
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/lesson.hpp owns the format.
#
# The speeds are the aeroplane own, from its Pilot's Notes through
# `assets/figures/mosquito-fb6.xml`; the heights are against where the stage
# began, so the exercise may be flown at any altitude.

name Climbs and descents in a wartime twin
teaches second-world-war

stage The climb
do Set the climbing power and hold the climbing speed
do Keep the engine temperatures inside their limits as she climbs
hold velocities/vc-kts climb-30 climb+30 Hold the climbing speed
until position/h-agl-ft >= start+900

stage Levelling off
do Lower the nose at the height you want and let the speed build
do Set the cruising power once the speed is there
until velocities/h-dot-fps <= 3.0

stage The descent
do Bring the power back and let the nose down to a steady rate
do Do not let her run away: this is a clean aeroplane and she will
hold velocities/vc-kts climb-30 climb+90 Hold the speed in the descent
until position/h-agl-ft <= start-500
